A heap which is full while C++ builds a list grows by an eighth, not by 4 (TeXmacs)

While a tmscm_builder exists, TeXmacs holds the collector (gc_off). When
the free cells then run out, new_cell cannot collect and grows the heap
with resize_heap: by 4 once the heap is 4M cells or more, as the free
cells are under half. What the builder still needs is small, but the
heap never shrinks: a heap of 8M cells (0.9 GB of memory) became 32M
(2.5 GB) in about half of the runs of the suites kbd-menu and search,
whenever a builder (tmg_tree_children of a tree) happened to run just
as the free list was used up (mgubi/texmacs#719). resize_heap_to takes
a negative size to mean "grow by that many cells"; the forced growth
now adds an eighth of the heap (64000 cells at least).

--- a/s7.c
+++ b/s7.c
@@ -8343,7 +8343,9 @@
 	    __func__, func, line, old_free, old_size, size, sc->gc_resize_heap_fraction, (s7_int)(floor(sc->heap_size * sc->gc_resize_heap_fraction)));
 #endif
 
-  if (size == 0)
+  if (size < 0)
+    sc->heap_size += (-size);            /* TeXmacs: grow by that many cells (see try_to_call_gc) */
+  else if (size == 0)
     {
       if ((old_free < old_size * sc->gc_resize_heap_by_4_fraction) &&
 	  (sc->max_heap_size > (sc->heap_size * 4)))
@@ -8455,7 +8457,11 @@
 #if s7_Debugging
       fprintf(stderr, "%s[%d]: forced resize from %s[%d]\n", __func__, __LINE__, func, line);
 #endif
-      resize_heap(sc);
+      /* TeXmacs: the collector is off (tmscm_builder) and the free cells are used up. What the builder still needs
+       *   is not known, but is small, and a heap never shrinks: by 4, a heap of 8M cells (0.9 GB of memory) became
+       *   32M (2.5 GB) when the free list ran out at the wrong moment. Grow by an eighth instead.
+       */
+      resize_heap_to(sc, -((sc->heap_size / 8) > 64000 ? (sc->heap_size / 8) : 64000));
     }
   else
     {
